    "text": "To determine the combined length of the CDs that James buys, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the length of the first two CDs.\n2. Calculate the length of the third CD.\n3. Add the lengths of all three CDs together.\n\nStep 1: The length of the first two CDs is given as 1.5 hours each. So, the total length of the first two CDs is:\n\\[ 1.5 \\text{ hours} + 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 2: The length of the third CD is twice the length of one of the first two CDs. Since one of the first two CDs is 1.5 hours long, the length of the third CD is:\n\\[ 2 \\times 1.5 \\text{ hours} = 3 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nStep 3: To find the combined length of all three CDs, we add the lengths of the first two CDs and the third CD:\n\\[ 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} + 3 \\text{ hours} = 9 \\text{ hours} \\]\n\nTherefore, the combined length of the CDs is \\(\\boxed{9}\\).",
